reast Cancer Prognostic, an RNA expression test for assessing the aggressiveness of breast cancer; Precise Tumor Molecular Profile, a genomic profiling test; Prequel Prenatal Screen, a prenatal screening test to screen chromosomal disorders in a fetus; Foresight Carrier Screen, a prenatal test for future parents to assess risk of passing on recessive genetic condition to offspring; SneakPeek Early Gender DNA, a non-invasive blood test that predicts the fetus's gender; FirstGene; and GeneSight Psychotropic Mental Health Medication, a DNA genotyping test to aid psychotropic drug selection for depression, anxiety, attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder, and other mental health conditions. It has a license collaboration with Illumina, Inc.; University of Texas M.D. Anderson Cancer Center; Mayo Foundation for Medical Education and Research; Children's Medical Center in Boston; Institut Curie and INSERM; and Eurobio Scientific SA. The company has a strategic alliance with SOPHiA GENETICS SA to advance new prostate cancer-specific genomic instability score technology for oncology approaches with AstraZeneca. The company was founded in 1991 and is headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Samraat S. Raha | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $305K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Myriad Genetics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $567M market cap on $824M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -19% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 70% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $14M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -52.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -36.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 47% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 67/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 178% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Myriad Genetics (MYGN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/myriad-genetics-mygn-q3-2026-185024000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793905042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Myriad Genetics (MYGN) shares skyrocket, what you need to know","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/mygn/news/why-up-down/myriad-genetics-mygn-shares-skyrocket-what-you-need-to-know-2","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895381.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Myriad outlines $780M-$790M 2026 revenue outlook following $210M Prenatal Health divestiture deal (NASDAQ:MYGN)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666813-myriad-outlines-780m-790m-2026-revenue-outlook-following-210m-prenatal-health-divestiture","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894852.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","m_and_a"]},{"title":"Myriad Genetics Inc (MYGN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Revenue Guidance Raised as ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/myriad-genetics-inc-mygn-q3-091307793.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793869987.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentimen